# third-party/compiled/ (the per-filetype `.yrc` + manifest.json) is a BUILD
# ARTIFACT and is not committed. A published traits bundle is assembled and
# served from R2, and that is the only path by which precompiled rules reach a
# client -- cleave loads them from the bundle's own third-party/compiled/, never
# from a git checkout. Committing them here shipped 27MB of binaries that no
# client read, and that went stale on any rule edit besides.
#
# Regenerate into the bundle with `make precompile` (verify with
# `make verify-precompile`) when preparing a publish. A local checkout needs
# nothing: cleave compiles from source on first use and caches the result
# outside the repo.
third-party/compiled/
samples/
